# the ELF image writer: an executable from the image record of a link
#
# every address, file offset and size comes from the layout record, and every
# byte of an output section from the relocated record, so the writer computes
# no address. it builds the ELF model the ELF writer turns into bytes. the
# header takes its machine, class and byte order from the architecture row,
# its e_flags, EI_OSABI and EI_ABIVERSION from the settled facts and traits,
# with the system row's OSABI where no input states one, and its entry from
# the entry symbol. a PT_LOAD maps each segment of the layout, PT_NOTE each
# run of loaded notes, PT_GNU_RELRO the run of sections read only once
# relocated, PT_GNU_PROPERTY the GNU property note, the vendor's
# program header its build attributes, and PT_GNU_STACK the stack, which is
# executable only when an input's stack section asks for it. the section
# headers list the output sections in image order, then the symbol table and
# the string tables. a link that needs what the image cannot hold yet is refused,
# naming what it needs.
#
# the GNU property note, the build attributes and the identification strings
# are sections the image makes from the settled record: its declarer sizes
# them before layout, and the writer fills the places layout gave them with
# the same bytes.

